e chardee  dockery  principal dockery  principal dockery i'm so happy to meet  you  how do you think that a good deed  grocery store  could work and benefit inside of your  school oh  wow so delay middle school we're about  90  um economically disadvantaged which  means most of our students receive free  and reduced lunch  a lot of our families are living in  low-income housing  from trailer home communities to budget  suites and some of them are actually  homeless so they do not have  access to just kind of fresh organic or  healthy  healthy foods just within their you know  within their immediate community  and i just i saw a principal love story  and even the pieces on kindness and  and empathy and just servant leadership  our students definitely need that  experience because they  do not have those experiences out you  know in their communities and they don't  travel outside of their you know their  two mile radius often  principal love um do you have any advice  may i ask since you've done it  so you got to have a champion for the  grocery store you got to have somebody  who  who believes in it sees the vision and  you just have to have  a you know the mindset that failure is  not an option  there will be things come up that you're  not expecting  but you just have to have a team with  you that is there to  to support you and to support the  students  hmm that sounds like really honest and  real world  advice find the right people and  expect the unexpected there's not a  reference for this  and um we wanted to help turn this dream  into a reality and spread the love so  here to join us is catherine oliveros  the vice president  of community health improvement at texas  health resources  and they are the largest non-profit  health system in north texas and their  program has been going  beyond the walls of their hospitals and  into their communities  hi catherine thank you so much for  joining us today  thank you drew it's great to join you  catherine i was won